    "result_text": "I've implemented the change. Let me summarize what was done.\n\n## Summary\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133) derived at creation.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` (which returned `\"GOLD\"`/`\"SILVER\"`/`\"BRONZE\"`) with `getMembershipLevel()` returning an `Integer`:\n   - starts at `1`\n   - `+1` when an email is present\n   - `+1` when `namesakeCount` is `0`\n   - capped at `3` via a `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` constant (level 4 reserved for tenure)\n   \n   The old household-driven `GOLD` logic and its `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE` constant were removed. The method lives in the `Owner` model alongside the other derived (`@Transient`) attributes, so MapStruct maps it into the response DTO automatically by name.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string/enum schema property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with `membershipLevel` in place of `membershipTier`.\n\n3. Cleaned up two now-stale Javadoc comments in `Owner.java` and `ClinicServiceImpl.java` that referenced the removed GOLD tier. `householdSize` itself is still captured/exposed as its own field \u2014 it just no longer drives membership.\n\n**On the audit line:** the spec noted \"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\" I checked `OwnerAuditLogger.logCreated` \u2014 it records `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` but never recorded the tier, so there was nothing to swap there.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` passes (owner with email + no namesakes \u2192 `membershipLevel` 3).",
